<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>Industrial generator maintenance in Nigeria is not housekeeping, it is capacity assurance. Where grid supply is unreliable, the genset carries the plant rather than backing it up, and it runs a duty cycle the original design assumed would be occasional. We maintain diesel and gas gensets from 100 kVA to multi megawatt sets across factories, processing plants, banks, hospitals, hotels and telecom facilities, covering scheduled servicing, top end and major overhauls, AVR and control faults, load bank testing, fuel systems and cooling.</p><p>The work is driven by measured condition rather than calendar habit. Every engagement opens with running hour data, oil and coolant sample results, the site load profile and a physical inspection of engine, alternator and control panel, so the scope you approve reflects the actual state of the set. You receive a written scope, parts list, outage window and price before any spanner is lifted, and where the wider power system is in question we start with a <a href="/power-plant-audit-nigeria/">power plant audit</a>.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Preventive Maintenance Contracts</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Scheduled visits tied to running hours with a calendar backstop, typically 250 and 500 hour service points and a 1,000 to 1,500 hour major inspection. Each visit closes with a signed report, oil analysis result and a list of items trending toward failure.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Top End and Major Overhauls</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Cylinder head, valve train, injector and turbocharger work at top end, through to liner, piston, bearing shell and crankshaft attention at major overhaul. Scope is set by compression, blow by and oil analysis data rather than by guesswork on hours alone.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">AVR, Governor and Control Faults</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">We trace voltage hunting, over voltage trips, load rejection faults and failure to build residual to the actual source, whether AVR, exciter, sensing circuit, actuator or controller. Panel wiring, ATS logic and protection settings are checked as one system.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Load Bank Testing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Resistive load bank testing at 25, 50, 75 and 100 percent steps proves the set will accept its rated block load and clears the effects of prolonged light running. Voltage, frequency, exhaust temperature, coolant temperature and fuel burn are logged at every step.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Fuel and Cooling Systems</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Fuel quality is the largest single cause of unplanned genset failure on Nigerian sites. We handle bulk tank cleaning, water and microbial contamination, filtration and polishing, injection system service, radiator recoring, thermostats and coolant chemistry.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #e3ded4;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(14,77,110,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Nunito Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#0A3D5C;margin:0 0 8px;">Black Start and Standby Readiness</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Where the genset carries critical load we verify start batteries and chargers, air start pressure, fuel priming, ATS transfer timing and first attempt start reliability over repeated cold starts. Findings are issued as a readiness report your operations team can work to.</p>
      </div>
</div>
